From: Can Us <me@canus.dev>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 18:22:54 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] Leave skinned/morphed renderables out of the SSR pass

SPECIAL_SSR_VARIANT (MNT|PCK|DEP) cannot carry SKN because
SPECIAL_SSR_MASK includes it, so setSkinning() turned the SSR variant of
a skinned or morphed renderable into MNT|PCK|DEP|SKN, which resolves as
a depth/picking variant. Its program does not match the SSR pass' render
target or per-view layout: GL tolerates it, Vulkan loses the device
(vkGetQueryPoolResults error=-4).

Skinned/morphed renderables now emit sentinel commands in the SSR pass
only; they are still drawn normally everywhere else.

diff --git a/filament/src/RenderPass.cpp b/filament/src/RenderPass.cpp
index af198953..31c6ff8a 100644
--- a/filament/src/RenderPass.cpp
+++ b/filament/src/RenderPass.cpp
@@ -621,6 +621,16 @@ RenderPass::Command* RenderPass::generateCommandsImpl(CommandTypeFlags extraFlag
 
         Variant renderableVariant{ variant };
 
+        // Lumina local patch (carried on top of v1.77.0):
+        // SPECIAL_SSR_VARIANT (MNT|PCK|DEP) cannot carry SKN -- SPECIAL_SSR_MASK includes it --
+        // so setSkinning() below would turn the SSR variant of a skinned or morphed renderable
+        // into MNT|PCK|DEP|SKN, which Variant resolves as a *depth/picking* variant. That
+        // program does not match the SSR pass' render target and per-view descriptor-set
+        // layout; GL tolerates it, Vulkan loses the device (vkGetQueryPoolResults error=-4).
+        // Until SSR gains skinning variants, skinned/morphed renderables are simply left out
+        // of the screen-space reflections pass (they are still drawn normally).
+        bool const skipInSsrPass = Variant::isSSRVariant(variant) && hasSkinningOrMorphing;
+
         // We can't have SSR and shadowing together by construction.
         assert_invariant(!Variant::isSSRVariant(variant) || !hasShadowing);
         renderableVariant.setShadowReceiver(soaVisibility[i].receiveShadows && hasShadowing);
@@ -673,9 +683,10 @@ RenderPass::Command* RenderPass::generateCommandsImpl(CommandTypeFlags extraFlag
          */
         for (auto const& primitive: primitives) {
             FMaterialInstance const* const mi = primitive.getMaterialInstance();
-            if (UTILS_UNLIKELY(!mi)) {
+            if (UTILS_UNLIKELY(!mi || skipInSsrPass)) {
                 // This can happen because RenderPrimitives can be initialized with
                 // a null MaterialInstance. In this case, skip the primitive.
+                // (Also taken for skinned/morphed renderables in the SSR pass, see above.)
                 if constexpr (isColorPass) {
                     curr->key = uint64_t(Pass::SENTINEL);
                     ++curr;
